WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:03.980
<b>Red Rum, Inc.</b>

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.980
This is our new target.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.940
Murder, Inc.

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.940
<b>Staff List</b>

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:06.940
Wasn't this guy in Fukuoka?

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.210
Saito.

00:00:08.810 --> 00:00:10.850
He went into hiding in Hakata.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:11.720
Huh.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.150
Are we disappearing him?

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.470
We can't let him reveal any secrets.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.080
What the hell does that mean?!

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:23.830
I'm saying you aren't going to 
make it outside this company.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.520
You're a nameless hitman, 
and you don't even have connections.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.300
This company only ever gives me shit jobs!

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.010
You're free to quit, if that's how you feel.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:36.930
Don't blame me if you end up regretting it.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.380
I won't regret it.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:45.020
Hurry up and hand over my severance pay.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:19.470
<b>#05  Tryouts</b>

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:30.120
<b>Kakyu Association Chairman   Longfang Wang</b>

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:30.120
Have we still not dealt 
with the Niwaka Samurai?

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.630
I apologize.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:36.640
He tried to mess with the brass. 
How much longer until he's dead?

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.840
It's a disgrace to our organization.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.300
We'll use an outside hitman 
to dispatch him quickly.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.870
Just give us a little time.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.020
Want some, Maru-chan?

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.270
Oh, thanks.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:57.130
Misaki-chan, can I have some?

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.110
Okay.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.080
Thanks.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.710
Practice matches... What a pain in the ass.

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:05.610
And why are you already in your uniform?

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:06.690
Lame.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:08.950
Hey, it looks badass!

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.040
Doesn't it?

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.220
I can't say I'd wear it on a train.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.500
See?

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.000
What? That's so mean.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:25.090
I appreciate the work Jiro gives me, 
but I want some work at my main job, too.

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:26.560
Why don't you use this, then?

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.770
<b>Shadyjob.com</b>

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:28.770
Shadyjob.com?

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:32.020
It's a site on the dark web that's 
well-known in underworld circles.

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:36.600
You should post on the "job search" 
forum. It'll be good marketing.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.070
You quit work, huh?

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:45.250
More like I've been absent without notice, 
so I've probably been fired by now.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:48.040
<i>Next stop, Kashii. Kashii.</i>

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.240
We're here.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.710
Oh, Lin-chan...

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:59.330
It gets shaky here. 
You shouldn't stand up yet.

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.300
You could've told me that earlier!

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.610
<b>Hakata 
Tonkotsu 
Ramens</b>

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:04.610
<b>Tenjin
Thunders</b>

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.610
Nice! A double!

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.950
Uh-oh...

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.120
Lin!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:30.780
Here!

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:35.360
What?!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.670
Oh, dear...

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:47.030
Safe!

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:50.310
What the hell are you doing?!

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:53.290
I keep telling you to throw at my chest!

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:55.690
Shut up, damn it, moron Ban!

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:57.500
You're the moron!

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.570
You let it roll right between your feet!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.720
What could I have done?

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.290
It took a bad hop!

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:05.810
It's not hard to predict a bad hop!

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:08.390
Know the state of the field
and put up a solid defense.

00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:09.580
It's common sense!

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.710
Whatever!

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.380
Watch your attitude!

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.080
<i>Ogura. Ogura.</i>

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:25.880
Gotta find a job.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:30.330
Maybe if I put a hit out on 
the agencies in this area...

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:33.240
Wasn't that pitcher from Nishi High wild?

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:34.580
I could never hit those pitches.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:35.910
I'm starving.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.560
<b>Ogura Kita 
High School</b>

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:05.880
Your early-game control is as terrible as ever.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:08.840
Hey. Long time, Sarucchi.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.550
Who are you?

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:14.100
What? That's pretty harsh!

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:17.170
I used to be your right-hand man.

00:06:17.170 --> 00:06:18.310
It's me.

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:19.560
Nitta Naoya.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.040
No biggie, Sarucchi!

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.440
Let's turn this around!

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:27.070
Nao...

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:29.510
You seem bummed out.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:32.580
Did you get laid off or something?

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:34.280
I didn't get laid off.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.460
I quit.

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:36.170
Yeah?

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:40.200
I heard it's a pretty good place 
to work. Murder, Inc., I mean.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.000
Hitman 
Consultant

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.000
<b>Nitta Naoya</b>

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.000
"Hitman Consultant"?

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.210
It's exactly as it sounds.
I'm a consultant for hitmen.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:51.220
Hitmen have all kinds of things they want.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:56.640
To make lots of money, to become 
famous, to do work that thrills them...

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:01.490
My job is to provide such hitmen 
with professional advice.

00:07:01.490 --> 00:07:04.060
I'm shrewder than you might think.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.070
Huh.

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:08.530
<b>Udon / Soba</b>

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.110
What a coincidence, though, huh?

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:12.780
A high school battery, working 
in the same industry again.

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:15.740
You knew I was an assassin?

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:21.400
I heard someone was leaving
Murder, Inc. and coming here.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:22.960
Why did you quit?

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:28.360
I got bored of killing weaklings.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.300
I want to go up against stronger targets.

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.480
I see.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.440
In that case, Fukuoka's 
the perfect place for you.

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:38.740
There are lots of strong people here.

00:07:38.740 --> 00:07:44.730
Such as the Niwaka Samurai, 
the hitmen hitman, for instance.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.190
Huh? Niwaka Samurai?

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:51.110
Hey, Sarucchi, want to work with me?

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:55.160
I'll make you Fukuoka's top hitman.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:57.870
Let's team up again.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.690
Like old times.

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.820
Wow, you're buying so much stuff.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.240
Yo.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:14.900
What's wrong with that?

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:18.590
I'm pissed right now, after getting 
yelled at by that baseball freak.

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:21.060
I don't know why you'd even 
come here, mushroom.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:25.700
Come on, it's not like I spend 
all my time in an internet café.

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:29.530
I'm meeting up with a client at a 
motsunabe place by the railway.

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:31.460
Work, huh?

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:32.820
Yup.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.180
Later.

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:38.780
I'm hungry.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:45.830
So I heard from one of my acquaintances 
that you're a good informant.

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:48.790
I want you to find this guy.

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:50.590
What's wrong?

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.530
Nothing, just that I've seen this face around.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:55.010
Who is he?

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.850
His name's Saito.

00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:58.620
He betrayed his organization.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:01.220
So you want me to find him 
and take care of him?

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:03.770
That's the idea. Can you find him?

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.610
Of course.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.170
What are you drawing?

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:16.950
Misaki's class is doing a play.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.080
Ta-da.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:21.110
Misaki is the Princess of 
the Mushroom Kingdom.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:25.910
I have to do the costume and 
wig myself. It's so much work.

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:29.630
Wow, you're a princess, Misaki? That's amazing.

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:30.630
Not really.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.660
My name was drawn, that's all.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.250
Done.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:40.140
<b>We do torture!</b>

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:40.140
<b>O   To extract information</b>

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:40.140
<b>O   To make them suffer</b>

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:40.140
<b>O   To cause them pain</b>

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:40.140
For all your torture needs!

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:40.140
Bargain torturers for hire     Email for quotes

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:36.530
"To extract information..."

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:37.520
"To make them suffer..."

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:38.430
"To cause them pain..."

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.450
"For all your torture needs!"

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:42.310
"Bargain torturers for hire."

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:44.340
"Email for quotes."

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:45.460
Nice.

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:50.100
Hey, please don't make my 
Misaki write such nasty stuff!

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:58.410
Keep

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:58.410
Out

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.780
<b>Staff Only</b>

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.240
Ta-da.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:03.190
Well?

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:06.460
I've prepared the perfect 
weapons for you, Sarucchi.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:09.420
What the hell is all this?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.180
Ninja weapons.

00:10:11.180 --> 00:10:13.380
A ninja sword, shuriken, kunai,

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:14.880
as well as claws, and—

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:16.840
Are you messing with me?!

00:10:16.840 --> 00:10:18.120
Not at all.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:21.460
There are samurai, so why not ninja hitmen?

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:24.470
It's punchy. People will remember you.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.720
Oh, and wear this on your head.

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:30.150
Your catchphrase is 
"I shall take your life now, sir."

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:32.710
What do you think? Awesome, right?

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:34.360
Hell no! You're messing with me!

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.720
Just give it a throw.

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:37.820
Here.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:55.420
Your early-game control is as terrible as ever.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:56.830
Shut up.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:11:00.680
I'm sure you'll be fine with some practice.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.120
With that said,

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:04.600
I'll give you this, too.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.450
What's all this?

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:10.060
It's a list of all the hitmen 
working in Kitakyushu.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:13.270
Pick a few of them to take out.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:18.210
Eventually, one of their organizations will 
take note of the mystery ninja hitman.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:21.450
<b>Ramen</b>

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:24.160
Please!

00:11:24.510 --> 00:11:26.550
I won't screw up like this again!

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:29.540
What can we say? They had a similar name.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:29.540
Hey!

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.620
Get lost!

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:36.670
<b>Gen-chan 
Oden / Ramen</b>

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:33.550
Never walk through these curtains again!

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.330
Oh, fine.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:38.580
The hell is his problem?

00:11:38.580 --> 00:11:40.750
Idiots everywhere.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:41.770
Shut up!

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.850
They killed someone totally different?

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:47.480
Yeah.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:50.740
Taking out the wrong person 
can be fatal in this business.

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:52.560
So I fired them.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.520
Not much you can do about that.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.090
Hey, boss, can I come in?

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:57.520
Welcome.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.540
What's wrong with you, Lin-chan?

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:02.250
You vanished as soon as the game was over.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.330
You've been wasting money again, huh?

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:08.920
Shut up. Are you going to lecture me again?

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:10.170
Again?

00:12:10.170 --> 00:12:11.710
Did I say something before?

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:14.570
You said plenty during the game.

00:12:14.570 --> 00:12:16.670
Something about the state 
of the field or whatever.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.900
That's not lecturing.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.430
It's advice you can apply 
to every part of your life.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:22.600
Huh?

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:23.980
Beer, please, boss.

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:25.910
And ramen. Firm noodles.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:27.070
All right.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:31.000
Ramen for me, too. Normal noodles.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.140
Sure.

00:12:35.800 --> 00:12:37.520
Oh, by the way, boss...

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:41.950
I'm going to take some time 
off work starting tomorrow.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.490
It's that time of year already, huh?

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:45.650
Yup.

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:48.110
I can't skip out on the Yamakasa.

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:50.450
"Yamakasa"? What's that?

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:53.590
You live in Hakata and you 
don't know what the Yamakasa is?

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:56.710
I'm talking about the Hakata Gion Yamakasa.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.960
That doesn't mean anything to me.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:02.170
It's a huge festival in Hakata.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:08.390
The men carry a float called the Kakiyama 
and run through the town of Hakata.

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:12.740
It happens every year 
from July 1st to the 15th.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:16.350
It's a traditional festival that 
goes back nearly 800 years.

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:20.690
In the Oiyama event on the last day,
seven teams, known as the Nagare,

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:25.820
carry a float that weighs a ton
five kilometers northward.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:29.540
What's so fun about that?

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:32.170
Banba's going to be in the Yamakasa, too.

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:35.250
He stops working around 
this time every year.

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:40.790
I just got rid of two people, though,
so it hurts to have Banba take a break.

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:44.410
Let Lin-chan have my work.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.740
Don't be stupid.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:50.010
I'm not working in place of someone 
who's taking off to a festival.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:52.920
Oh, yeah, that's right...

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:55.480
I should have known it would 
be too much for you.

00:13:57.050 --> 00:14:00.570
My work would probably still 
be too much of a burden.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:01.650
What the hell?

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:04.840
If that's what you think, fine. I'll do it!

00:14:05.460 --> 00:14:07.860
Is that what you thought I'd say?

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:11.320
I'm not falling for that, idiot.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:15.850
You've grown up, Lin.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:17.290
Give me some oden, old man.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:18.930
Egg and daikon radish.

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:19.810
All right.

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:22.210
That wasn't cute.

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.470
<b>A Few Days Later</b>

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:35.430
What does this guy want?!

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:38.500
Shit...

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.070
Don't! No!

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:46.940
Huh?

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:48.900
You took out all of them?

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.130
They were all wusses.

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:53.620
This is no different from 
when I was at the company.

00:14:53.620 --> 00:14:55.890
Don't be in such a hurry.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:57.040
Huh?

00:14:57.040 --> 00:15:00.490
I've got someone scouting the ninja hitman.

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:03.880
It's a transnational mafia startup 
called Kakyu Association.

00:15:04.330 --> 00:15:06.520
I've made plans to meet 
with their brass tomorrow.

00:15:06.980 --> 00:15:09.550
A transnational mafia, huh?

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:14.480
It looks like they're after that hitmen hitman.

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:15.760
The Niwaka Samurai.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:18.730
The Niwaka Samurai?

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:28.070
Yo, Enokida-kun.

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:30.290
Oh, Banba-san.

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:33.550
What a coincidence, seeing you here.

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:35.030
On your way home from the internet café?

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:38.670
Again, it's not like I spend my 
entire life at the internet café.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:41.000
I have a meeting with a client right now.

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:43.250
Are you in the Yamakasa?

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.700
Yup.

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:46.920
I just finished today's events.

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:49.050
Don't overdo it.

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:50.420
Oh, yeah...

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:54.830
So Enokida-kun gave me his newest piece.

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:57.890
A redback spider phone strap.

00:15:58.230 --> 00:15:59.540
Um...

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:00.820
Huh? Where do I put it?

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:03.100
I don't need that creepy shit on my phone!

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:05.670
Put it on your own old-school phone!

00:16:05.670 --> 00:16:06.960
Huh? What?

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.650
Don't breathe your booze breath on me.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:12.540
You've been at it every night this week.

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:14.530
You're getting sloppy.

00:16:14.970 --> 00:16:16.450
There. Done.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.970
Don't fall asleep here!

00:16:18.970 --> 00:16:20.700
Go sleep on a bed!

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:23.420
Thank you.

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:26.130
Next customer, please.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.420
Here.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:29.950
The address of this so-called Saito-kun.

00:16:29.950 --> 00:16:32.950
I'm shocked he lives under his actual name.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:37.870
Here's your reward, as promised.

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:39.470
I'll ask you again if I ever need anything.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.930
Are you going to kill him right away?

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:43.140
Yeah.

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:45.900
Later.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:02.330
<i>Please leave a message after the beep.</i>

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:06.290
Hello? Saito-kun?

00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:11.830
I gotta go take a nap.

00:17:13.270 --> 00:17:15.660
<i>Hello? Saito-kun?</i>

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:17.220
<i>It's me, Enokida.</i>

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:21.110
<i>I just gave your address to a hitman.</i>

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:24.680
<i>He's on his way to kill you.</i>

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:25.940
<i>Okay, thanks.</i>

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:27.250
Huh?!

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:34.100
Gwen-san?! Shit!

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:36.990
It's him! Damn it!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.450
Pick up, pick up, please!

00:17:43.890 --> 00:17:45.910
Banba-san! Help me!

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:48.430
Saito? What's up?

00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:50.630
<i>Huh? Lin-san? Where's Banba-san?</i>

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:52.840
He's sleeping. Snoring away.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.900
<i>You'll do, then, Lin-san!</i>

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:56.300
What do you mean, "I'll do"?

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:57.630
I'm being chased!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:59.840
By a hitman from Murder, Inc.!

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:00.890
From Tokyo!

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:03.400
I think I got the gist.

00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:04.350
Where are you?

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:07.100
I'm headed toward Hakata Station.

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:08.610
<i>Let's meet at the station.</i>

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:09.770
<i>I'll be right there.</i>

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:17.820
I'm here.

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:18.950
Where are you, Saito?

00:18:19.310 --> 00:18:22.410
I'm hiding in the train to Kokura on track 3.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:25.590
<i>Kokura? The one we were on?</i>

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:27.370
Yeah. The second car.

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:28.900
<i>Shit, he's getting on!</i>

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:30.580
Just stay hidden!

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:48.230
Saito-kun, I know you're here.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.890
Gwen-san.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:53.400
Long time no see.

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.490
Glad to see you're doing well.

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:58.300
You look slightly more 
handsome than before, even.

00:18:58.300 --> 00:19:00.070
Th-Thanks.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:03.530
You should use that face 
for your funeral photo.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.060
W-Wait a second!

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.250
Why do I need to die?

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:10.440
You know what our company does, don't you?

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:13.480
I'm just following my orders to kill you.

00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:27.350
Lin-san!

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:31.020
Shit...

00:19:35.090 --> 00:19:36.480
Who are you?

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:40.210
I'm just a passing hitman.

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:43.160
You should let that wimp be.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:45.170
I can't do that.

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:47.350
This is my job.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:49.870
I stop at nothing.

00:19:52.550 --> 00:19:53.970
Here!

00:20:00.070 --> 00:20:01.080
A fake?

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:02.470
Lin-san!

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:03.820
Shoot.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:05.390
A knife pistol, huh?

00:20:05.910 --> 00:20:07.480
That's unusual.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:09.770
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.880
<i>I need to make it through this somehow.</i>

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:15.440
Know the state of the field
and put up a solid defense.

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:16.980
It's common sense!

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:21.030
<i>Know the state of the field...</i>

00:20:23.160 --> 00:20:26.140
You're from Tokyo, aren't you?

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:26.920
Yeah.

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:28.410
You must not know, then...

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:30.300
<i>Next stop: Kashii.</i>

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:31.520
This train...

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:32.460
At this stop...

00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:36.290
gets shaky!

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:46.580
<i>Kashii.</i>

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:48.520
<i>The doors on the right side will open.</i>

00:20:48.980 --> 00:20:52.480
<i>Please mind your step when the doors open.</i>

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:56.760
That baseball freak's advice 
actually came in handy.

00:20:56.760 --> 00:20:57.440
Huh?

00:20:58.200 --> 00:20:59.780
Never mind.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:00.770
We're going home.

00:21:02.670 --> 00:21:05.320
<b>Kakyu Association's Hakata Headquarters</b>

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:08.530
So you're the Submarine 
Ninja from the rumors?

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:11.010
Huh? "Submarine Ninja"?

00:21:11.590 --> 00:21:15.000
Isn't that what they call a 
really low pitch in baseball?

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:18.130
I hear that's the way you throw your shuriken.

00:21:18.730 --> 00:21:20.710
Sure, I guess.

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:23.620
You'd better not be the one 
spreading that nickname.

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:25.430
Of course not.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:29.510
So can you kill the Niwaka Samurai?

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:32.730
He's strong, is he?

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:35.520
Yeah, he's quite formidable.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:38.390
Leave him to me, then.

00:22:36.910 --> 00:22:39.360
Are you the so-called Niwaka Samurai?

00:22:39.360 --> 00:22:40.320
Must have been rough.

00:22:40.320 --> 00:22:41.740
Hey, boss?

00:22:41.740 --> 00:22:42.500
What's wrong?

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:43.960
It was rough.

00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:45.300
I was just worried.

00:23:09.830 --> 00:23:10.950
Cheers.

00:23:11.270 --> 00:23:13.910
We got the contract.

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:17.620
How do we find out where the 
Niwaka Samurai is, though?

00:23:17.620 --> 00:23:21.240
I'll ask my connections to find his agency.

00:23:21.240 --> 00:23:24.040
Might take a while, though.

00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:25.340
Thanks.

00:23:25.650 --> 00:23:28.280
100 million yen for just one hit, huh?

00:23:28.280 --> 00:23:30.010
That's pretty generous.

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:33.800
He must have really done a 
number on their reputation.

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:41.020
#06 Pinch Hitter
